### Get all employees
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Accept: application/json

###
### Search employees with server-side filters and pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/search?keyword=Li&deptId=1&positionId=1&status=active&page=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

###
### Get employee detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/1/detail
Accept: application/json

###
### Create employee
### Change phone/email before re-running to avoid unique constraint conflicts.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "empName": "Test Employee",
  "gender": "male",
  "age": 23,
  "phone": "13800000009",
  "email": "testemployee@test.com",
  "hireDate": "2026-04-22",
  "deptId": 1,
  "positionId": 1,
  "status": "active",
  "leaveDate": null
}

###
### Update employee
### Replace 3 with the actual empId returned by GET/POST.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/3
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "empName": "Test Employee Updated",
  "gender": "male",
  "age": 24,
  "phone": "13800000019",
  "email": "testemployee-updated@test.com",
  "hireDate": "2026-04-22",
  "deptId": 1,
  "positionId": 1,
  "status": "active",
  "leaveDate": null
}

###
### Regularize probation employee
### Replace 3 with an employee whose status is probation.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/3/regularize
Accept: application/json

###
### Resign employee
### Replace 3 with the actual empId.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/3/resign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "leaveDate": "2026-05-31"
}

###
### Delete employee
### Replace 3 with the actual empId you want to delete.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/3
Accept: application/json

###
### Export employees CSV
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/export/employees.csv
Accept: text/csv
